    basic: "Maintain the rhythm. If you lose the beat of the chant, you will be late to react when the match occurs. Focus on the dealer's hand movement.",
    intermediate: "Peripheral Vision: Don't stare at the center. Watch the player whose turn it is next. If you see them flinching to slap, you should slap too.",
    advanced: "Rhythmic Deception: Some high-level variants allow the current player to pause slightly or speed up their flip to bait opponents into a 'fake' slap (foul).",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Keep your slapping hand close to the table edge, not in your lap.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "In drinking variants, the person who takes the pile also 'takes a sip'.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Pay attention when the chant resets from Ace back to Seven; this is the most common moment for reaction errors.',
      },
